{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-011", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Amazon, Nadara switch on 277 MW agrivoltaic facility in Italy", "content": "<p>Nadara has completed the 227 MW Big Fish agrivoltaic project in Sicily, backed by a 156 MW PPA with Amazon and described by the developer as Italy’s largest agrivoltaic facility. The 400-hectare project was approved with a 20 MW/40 MWh battery energy storage system.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/amazon-nadara-switch-on-277-mw-agricoltaic-facility-in-italy/\">Amazon, Nadara switch on 277 MW agrivoltaic facility in Italy</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://ww", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/amazon-nadara-switch-on-277-mw-agricoltaic-facility-in-italy/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-012", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Ukraine adds 1.1 GW of solar in H1", "content": "<p>Analysis from the Solar Energy Association of Ukraine estimates the country's solar capacity reached up to 9.7 GW by mid-2026.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/ukraine-adds-1-1-gw-of-solar-in-h1/\">Ukraine adds 1.1 GW of solar in H1</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/ukraine-adds-1-1-gw-of-solar-in-h1/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-013", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Korea tenders 6.6 GWh of six-hour storage under 15-year contracts", "content": "<p>The Korea Power Exchange has launched its 2026 ESS tender for 1.18 GW of six-hour storage, targeting 1.1 GW on mainland Korea and 80 MW on Jeju, with projects due by February 2029. Bids will be assessed 50% on price and 50% on non-price factors, including fire safety, grid-forming capability, supply-chain resilience, Korean economic contribution, maintenance, recycling, and project experience.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/south-korea-tenders-6-6-gwh-of-six-h", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/south-korea-tenders-6-6-gwh-of-six-hour-storage-under-15-year-contracts/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-014", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Modified consumer camera can measure solar cell open-circuit voltage", "content": "<p>German researchers have modified and calibrated a low-cost consumer camera to quantitatively measure electroluminescence from silicon solar cells and modules. The method determines external luminescent quantum efficiency and uses it to derive the corresponding open-circuit voltage</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/modified-consumer-camera-can-measure-solar-cell-open-circuit-voltage/\">Modified consumer camera can measure solar cell open-circuit voltage</a> appeare", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/modified-consumer-camera-can-measure-solar-cell-open-circuit-voltage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-015", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ACEN relinquishes Philippine solar projects over land, access issues", "content": "<p>Land acquisition and site-access problems have led Philippine renewables developer ACEN to abandon two early-stage solar projects with a combined potential capacity of about 456 MW.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/acen-relinquishes-philippine-solar-projects-over-land-access-issues/\">ACEN relinquishes Philippine solar projects over land, access issues</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/acen-relinquishes-philippine-solar-projects-over-land-access-issues/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-23-016", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Canadian province announces PV panel recycling fee", "content": "<p>The government of Alberta is introducing a fee of CAN 14 ($15.99) to each new solar panel supplied in the province beginning October 1. It says the money raised will go towards collecting, transporting and recycling panels once they reach end of life.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/canadian-province-announces-pv-panel-recycling-fee/\">Canadian province announces PV panel recycling fee</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Globa", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/canadian-province-announces-pv-panel-recycling-fee/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "sungrow-2026-09-23-017", "date": "2026-09-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["sungrow"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sungrow brings PowerHarbor to Benelux homes for more value, less complexity", "content": "<p>With net metering ending in the Netherlands on January 1, 2027, households with rooftop solar are rethinking how to use the electricity they generate. PowerHarbor is designed for homeowners considering storage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/sungrow-brings-powerharbor-to-benelux-homes-for-more-value-less-complexity/\">Sungrow brings PowerHarbor to Benelux homes for more value, less complexity</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazi", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/23/sungrow-brings-powerharbor-to-benelux-homes-for-more-value-less-complexity/", "type": "rss"}]}
